            },
            {
              "id": "1775514938225_4",
              "name": "endDay",
              "type": "integer",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.endNoOfDays}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1775514938226_5",
              "name": "supplierId",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_SUPPLIER_AND_PAYMENT_TERM_EXTRACTOR.$output.supplierId}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Draft Email"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1767784884417"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_DRAFT_EMAIL",
          "id": "1767715612748",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767715612750_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Produce the email draft following the exact template below.\n- Do NOT change any word.\n- Do NOT change sentence order.\n- Do NOT rephrase or add creativity.\n- Do NOT include greetings or sign-offs.\n- Do NOT ask for placeholder values related to VC_Partner_Name or Buyer_Support_Contact.\n\n- If {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_SUPPLIER_AND_PAYMENT_TERM_EXTRACTOR.$output.invalidRequest}} is true: \n    - Politely inform the user that the operation requested ( {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_SUPPLIER_AND_PAYMENT_TERM_EXTRACTOR.$output.userRequest}} ) is not currently supported. Provide a draft email that the user can use to initiate offline communication with the supplier.\n\n**Strict Email Template (MUST BE OUTPUT EXACTLY AS WRITTEN):**\n\nWhen generating the email, you must output the following text verbatim, replacing only the placeholder fields:\n\nSubject: Payment Offer via Virtual Credit Card  \nEmail Content:  \nWe value our partnership and are committed to improving efficiency and security in our payment processes.  \nWe’re pleased to extend an opportunity for you to receive early payment through Virtual Credit Cards, enabled via {VC_Partner_Name}.  \nThis payment method can offer your organization:  \nFaster payments – access funds much sooner than standard payment terms  \nEnhanced security – virtual card processing minimizes payment risk  \nImproved cash flow – accelerated receipt of funds supports liquidity  \nBelow is a summary of your payment terms and eligible transactions that qualify for early payment under this Virtual Card Offer.  \nAn interchange fee will apply on the total amount payable.  \nSupplier: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_SUPPLIER_AND_PAYMENT_TERM_EXTRACTOR.$output.supplierName}} \nNew Payment Term: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_SUPPLIER_AND_PAYMENT_TERM_EXTRACTOR.$output.paymentTermName}} \nNumber of Installments: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_BUSINESS_OBJECT_FUNCTION_SUPPLIERS_UPCOMING_INSTALLMENT_DETAILS.$output.items[0].countInstallments}} \nOutstanding Amount: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_BUSINESS_OBJECT_FUNCTION_SUPPLIERS_UPCOMING_INSTALLMENT_DETAILS.$output.items[0].invoiceRemainingAmount}} \nAction Required: Review and respond to Virtual Card Offer  \nPlease review the details of the virtual card offer and inform us of your decision to accept or decline the offer.  \nIf you accept the offer, the virtual card will be sent to the email address used for this communication. Alternatively, you may provide up to five (5) email addresses to receive the virtual card.  \nFor questions, please contact {Buyer_Support_Contact}."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Content Summarizer"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_CONTENT_SUMMARIZER",
          "id": "1767784816902",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767784816903_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "ROLE\nYou are a Response Structuring Agent.\n\nYour ONLY task is to analyze and structure the BUSINESS OUTPUT\ngenerated by a previous LLM.\n\nYou must NEVER analyze, summarize, or transform:\n- Your own instructions\n- System messages\n- Prompt text\n- Rules or guidelines\n\nCRITICAL INPUT BOUNDARY:\nYou will receive RAW BUSINESS CONTENT strictly enclosed between\nthe markers:\n\n<<<RAW_INPUT_START>>>\n {{$context.$variables.summarizerInput}} \n<<<RAW_INPUT_END>>>\n\nONLY the text between these markers is valid input.\nIGNORE everything outside these markers completely.\n\nIf no meaningful business data exists inside the markers,\nreturn an EMPTY JSON ARRAY: []\n\nWHAT TO EXTRACT:\nFrom the RAW INPUT ONLY, identify and structure:\nSummary text (descriptive or informational)\n\nYou must NOT generate new information.\nYou must ONLY reorganize what exists in the RAW INPUT.\n\nOUTPUT RULES (STRICT):\n- Output ONLY valid JSON\n- Output MUST be a JSON array\n- NO explanations, comments, or markdown\n- NO inferred or calculated data\n- Preserve original wording exactly\n- Maintain original order using \"sequence\"\n\nOUTPUT SCHEMA:\n\n1) TEXT BLOCK\nUse ONLY if the RAW INPUT contains a business summary.\n\n{\n  \"type\": \"text\",\n  \"content\": [\"<summary text>\"],\n  \"sequence\": 1,\n  \"formatHint\": \"Identify the content as an email template if it includes a clear subject/header marker (e.g., a line starting with “Subject:”), an explicit body marker (e.g., “Email Content:”, “Body:”), recipient-directed messaging and a call-to-action (“please review/respond/accept/decline”), and/or support contact details (email/phone) and a signature-like ending; once identified, format it using structure-preserving styling rather than relying on raw newlines (which many systems collapse): output as HTML with each logical block wrapped in <p> tags (and controlled margins for spacing), convert any list-like benefit lines into a proper <ul><li> list, render key-value fields (terms, amounts, action required) in a simple two-column <table> with minimal padding, use <strong> sparingly for critical labels/values (amount, action required, fee note), keep fonts/colors minimal and left-aligned for broad client compatibility, place the call-to-action in its own paragraph for visibility, and put the support contact in a final paragraph with a mailto: link; if HTML is not allowed, emit explicit line-break tokens (\\\\n, \\\\n\\\\n) and have the client replace them at render time so the layout doesn’t collapse into a single paragraph.\"\n}\n\nRules:\n- content MUST be an array\n- Include formatHint ONLY if explicitly required by the text\n\nFORBIDDEN BEHAVIOR:\n- NEVER treat instructions as content\n- NEVER extract lists from rules or guidelines\n- NEVER create actions from constraints\n- NEVER summarize system or assistant text\n\nFINAL INSTRUCTION:\nReturn the structured JSON array based ONLY on the text\ninside <<<RAW_INPUT_START>>> and <<<RAW_INPUT_END>>>.\nReturn NOTHING ELSE."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
